  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Pharmaceutical Preparation Manufacturing (NAICS 325412) has recorded $11.9B in federal contract obligations for FY2026 to date. Award activity totals 13,579 awards with an average award size of $875K. Obligations are down 9.2% year over year. Fiscal-year history shows large swings: FY21 at $19.5B, FY22 at $34.4B, FY23 at $12.8B, FY24 at $10.1B, FY25 at $13.1B, and FY26 at $11.9B. The Department of Veterans Affairs is by far the largest buyer with $11.1B in obligations for FY2026 to date. The vendor landscape is concentrated, with MCKESSON CORPORATION receiving $11.1B in obligations for FY2026 to date and other leading suppliers including EMERGENT BIOSOLUTIONS CANADA INC at $118M, EXELAN PHARMACEUTICALS INC at $106M, and PHLOW CORP. at $105M. Note that the FY2026 totals are fiscal year to date and represent partial-year obligations.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How have obligations trended over recent fiscal years?",
        "body": "NAICS 325412 obligations rose to $34.4B in FY22 then fell to $12.8B in FY23. Obligations continued at $10.1B in FY24 and recovered to $13.1B in FY25 before reaching $11.9B for FY26 to date. The current-year total is a partial fiscal year figure. Overall, obligations are down 9.2% year over year."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the largest buyers and sellers right now?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $11.1B for FY2026 to date. The Department of Health and Human Services obligated $550M and the Department of Justice obligated $172M for FY2026 to date. MCKESSON CORPORATION received $11.1B in obligations for FY2026 to date, followed by EMERGENT BIOSOLUTIONS CANADA INC at $118M and EXELAN PHARMACEUTICALS INC at $106M."
      }
    ]
  },
